Test non-collinear Fe in LCAO basis with multiple k points, moments along +-y.

This is scf_angle_spin4 with the initial moments globally rotated by 90 degrees
about z (+-x -> +-y). Without spin-orbit coupling the spin frame is decoupled
from the lattice, so every result here must equal the scf_angle_spin4 reference
exactly.

The y channel is the only one that can go wrong on its own: m_x and m_z are read
off the real part of the spinor density-matrix block and are invariant under the
conjugation convention of that block, while m_y reads the imaginary part. The
+-x case therefore cannot detect a sign error in the sigma_y loop between the
Hamiltonian assembly (clx_j in merge_hr_part_to_hR) and the density extraction
(func_xyz_to_updown). See issues #7759 and #7831, and PRs #7513, #7664, #7832.
